WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.796 --> 00:00:06.757
Bradley better get on board and
it’s gotta happen in the next

00:00:06.757 --> 00:00:09.718
couple of days or we got some
hard decisions to make.

00:00:09.718 --> 00:00:10.677
Hard for you at least.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.680
We were looking
for a character who

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.891
would be able to banter with
Billy. In my head

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:17.851
the goal of those
characters they would

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:20.729
have these difficulties but they
would forge a relationship.

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:23.607
With Stella she'd need to be
as smart as her elders,

00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:26.526
but with a very different
sensibility and when you meet

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.445
Greta you'd see she had all that.

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:33.659
I don’t take it lightly to be
able to have this opportunity

00:00:33.659 --> 00:00:38.914
to show a young Asian American
woman in a position in power

00:00:38.914 --> 00:00:41.792
It’s happening in life,
so we need to show it.

00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:45.254
And to get to do it
with these people who I love

00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:46.255
It’s incredible.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.507
Well I wanna welcome back 
Alex Levy

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:50.425
When we did that dinner
scene that was the

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.970
first time that all of us
had been together

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.471
since the pandemic began.

00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:57.808
I missed the cast, I missed not
being able to see them,

00:00:57.808 --> 00:01:00.894
so when I get to see their
faces it’s so nice.

00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:03.355
To play the scene that is about

00:01:03.355 --> 00:01:05.983
a reunification I found
very rewarding.

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:08.193
You think Trump is innocent?

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:11.280
That- that’s not the point, the
point is that it’s a charade

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.448
The way Yanko is
being judged for his

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:15.909
political ideas is
very illuminating.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.077
Are we even allowed to have

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.954
conflicting opinions anymore?

00:01:18.954 --> 00:01:21.248
One of the great things that
Kerry has done this season

00:01:21.248 --> 00:01:23.917
highlight that as a society we
want to put people in boxes

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:27.087
How much will it cost for you to
get off my front step?

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.799
It's a complex set of
emotions when

00:01:30.841 --> 00:01:33.343
you’re dealing with this
character who has done these

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:37.055
terrible things and then they
come back and you’re wondering,

00:01:37.055 --> 00:01:40.833
am I being asked
to just hate this person,

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:43.687
am I being asked to feel for
them now?

00:01:43.687 --> 00:01:46.648
And I think that is going to be
left up to the viewer.

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:48.066
I'm really sorry Daniel.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.027
Apology not accepted.

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:53.280
I remember thinking "God, he
really was not hiding it -- 

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:54.197
at all."

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:56.325
That was one of the first
scenes where we are

00:01:56.325 --> 00:02:00.412
reminded that everyone
in this environment is

00:02:00.412 --> 00:02:01.872
really really ambitious.

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:05.751
Winning is a theme In
our storytelling.

00:02:05.751 --> 00:02:08.545
Cory wants to win,
Mia wants to win.

00:02:08.545 --> 00:02:11.423
They all want to win,
the journey is getting there.

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:12.674
(numerous) Cheers!

